    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "04d933a1_31a3ebbf",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 43,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-22T17:31:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With what byte value?  Seems like we should reserve an entry type for this.\n\nOr do you mean that the entry size itself is padded?\n\nOr do you assume that all readers have some external way of knowing the flash programming alignment?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 43,
        "startChar": 56,
        "endLine": 43,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "ccd6305832b073c150912291ac9d4ccaeb63adaa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bc44e46a_e0cc9b32",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 43,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-22T18:08:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes, log entries are padded to be of the integer size of flash minimal write size units. It does not matter which byte value is used actually.\n\nCan you suggest how to make this comment clearer?",
      "parentUuid": "04d933a1_31a3ebbf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 43,
        "startChar": 56,
        "endLine": 43,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "ccd6305832b073c150912291ac9d4ccaeb63adaa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2f59a53e_2c07d15b",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 43,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-22T19:11:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this expresses your intent:\n\nLog entries are always aligned to a multiple of the physical flash write size.  It is assumed that the reader and writer both know that size.  Bytes between the end of one entry and the start of the next one have undefined value and are not examined by the reader.\n\nThough I think this would be safer:\n\nLog entries may be padded to a multiple of the physical flash write size by appending bytes with the value FLASH_LOG_PAD, which is a reserved entry type.  This enables a reader which does not know the physical flash write size to parse log entries from a flash page.\n\nThat also allows compaction to be more efficient.  Compacted entries could be completely byte-packed since they\u0027re all written at once.  New entries written after that can be padded to the write size.",
      "parentUuid": "bc44e46a_e0cc9b32",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 43,
        "startChar": 56,
        "endLine": 43,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "ccd6305832b073c150912291ac9d4ccaeb63adaa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d774a8a8_f31c1df0",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 64,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-22T17:31:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems risky for events logged from a panic handler.  Perhaps those should not attempt compaction?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 64,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 64,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "ccd6305832b073c150912291ac9d4ccaeb63adaa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a83fe44_746b3d1b",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 64,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-22T18:08:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In fact this log facility as presented will not help to log panics, because flash driver usually uses os services (interrupts, events, etc).\n\nTo make this usable for panics we\u0027d need to add a single thread mode the flash driver.",
      "parentUuid": "d774a8a8_f31c1df0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 64,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 64,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "ccd6305832b073c150912291ac9d4ccaeb63adaa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
